<article class="env-remark" id="05TG">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05TG">Remark <span data-tag="05TG">7.7.2.6</span> <span class="named">(Isomorphism Invariance)</span>.</a> In the situation of Definition <a data-tag="05TJ" href="/tag/05TJ">7.7.2.5</a>, suppose that $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ is an $\infty $-category. Then the condition that $F: K^{\triangleright } \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ is an effective descent diagram for $U$ depends only on the isomorphism class of $F$ (as an object of the $\infty $-category $\operatorname{Fun}( K^{\triangleright }, \operatorname{\mathcal{C}})$). This follows from the characterization given in Remark <a data-tag="05TF" href="/tag/05TF">7.7.2.3</a> (together with Corollary <a data-tag="02K1" href="/tag/02K1">7.1.3.19</a>). </p>
